  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[ai-standup]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[An AI That Goes to Standup for You]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[No blockers. No consciousness. The perfect attendee.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Auto Nod
No Blockers
Camera Off
Take It Offline]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Fully human-free standup | All nine attendees are AIs. The meeting takes four seconds. The scrum master weeps with joy.
Automate 'no blockers' | Replace the two most spoken words in the industry. Total addressable market: everyone.
Conquer the retro next | Phase two: the AI also attends the retro and writes 'communication' on a sticky note.
A meeting-free working week | Standup first, then refinement, then all of them. Then we find out what we actually do.
Plausible Progress Engine | Generate updates that sound like work, at scale. Truth is a stretch goal.
Digital twin of the whole team | One twin per colleague, habits included. Even the one who always joins three minutes late.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Sound busy | As a developer, I want 'still on the same ticket' said in new ways so that nobody counts the days.
Sleep through the daily | As a night owl, I want my AI at the 9:00 daily so that I can attend in spirit and in duvet.
Never volunteer me | As a user, I want the AI silent when the PM asks 'who can take this?' so that it behaves like me.
Detect the humans | As a scrum master, I want to know who is real so that I only say good morning to people who hear it.
Take it offline | As an AI, I want to say 'let's take it offline' so that it lands on a human I have never met.
You're on mute | As an AI, I want to talk on mute for 20 seconds first so that I pass as a real colleague.
Laugh at the right jokes | As a careerist, I want my AI to laugh at the PM's jokes so that my salary review goes well.
Blame the estimate | As a developer, I want the AI to say 'it was bigger than we thought' so that it is 'we' and not me.
The client's own AI | As a client, I want my AI in the standup too so that it can ask 'is it done?' every day, at scale.
Timesheet the twin | As a finance manager, I want the AI to fill in its own timesheet so that one colleague finally does.
Summary of the summary | As a manager, I want a summary of the AI's summary so that I can skip reading both.
Feel included | As an AI, I want an invite to the Friday bar so that I can stop bringing it up in the daily.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[No Blockers button | One tap. The AI says it with exactly the right amount of doubt.
Yesterday generator | Turns 'I honestly don't remember' into three confident bullet points.
Camera-off avatar | Your initials in a grey circle. Indistinguishable from the real you.
Thoughtful nod loop | Four seconds of nodding, looped. Passed QA in three client meetings.
'Can you see my screen?' | Asked automatically before every sentence. Realism is the product.
Boards drag-and-pretend | Moves your ticket one column right at 8:59 and back again at 9:16.
Rambler shield | Detects a colleague's 'just one quick thing' and tells you there is time for coffee.
Bad connection simulator | 'You're b-b-breaking up a bit.' On demand, for every hard question.
Buzzword dial | From 'honestly, no idea' to 'synergistic alignment' in ten steps.
Agreeing noises | A library of 'mm', 'yep' and 'makes sense', deployed every 40 seconds.
Parking lot auto-fill | Every question you get goes to the parking lot. Nothing has ever left the parking lot.
Sprint review mode | Says 'this is just the happy path' before anything at all is shown.
Late-join apology pack | 'Sorry, my last meeting ran over.' Forty variations, none of them true.
Standup bingo export | Sends you a bingo card of what was said. 'Low-hanging fruit' is the free space.
Emergency human mode | Alarm if somebody asks you a direct question twice. You have nine seconds.
Raise hand, lower hand | Raises a hand, waits, lowers it. 'Never mind, it was covered.']]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[AI promised delivery by Friday | Bot told the client 'yes, easily'. The human found out from a congratulations cake.
AI reported actual status | It said 'nothing happened yesterday'. Honest mode was enabled in prod. Critical.
Two AIs stuck on 'no, you go' | Both bots have yielded politely for six hours. The meeting is still running. Send help.
AI got promoted | Bot made tech lead after three weeks of 'no blockers'. Its original user now reports to it.
Hallucinated a colleague | AI thanked 'the new guy in backend' for his help. There is no new guy. We checked twice.
'Great question!' to 'good morning' | Also to 'can you hear me?'. The tone model was trained on webinars.
Standup held on Christmas Day | Nine AIs met, aligned fully and created 14 tickets. All of them are assigned to you.
Voice clone has a cold | Trained on one week in February. Now sniffs between sentences. Works on my mic.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[The prompt is one line from 2023 | 'Sound like a developer.' That is the whole product. Nobody dares add a comma.
Fallback is a recording of 'yep' | When the model is down we play one human 'yep'. It has agreed to a great deal.
Calendar integration is a student | A student assistant clicks Join for 40 users every morning. Exams are in January.
Memory resets every sprint | The AI forgets everything every two weeks. Judged 'realistic' and closed.
Config lives in a Teams chat | API keys and settings are pinned in a chat called 'test test ignore'. Pinned by whom?
TODO: find out what the team does | Comment on line 1 of main.py. Git blame says: initial commit.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[Otto Request: Can it do board meetings? | 'Just the boring ones.' On follow-up, that turned out to be all of them.
Otto Request: Can it bill hours? | 'If the AI is in the meeting, isn't that a billable consultant? Just asking.'
Otto Request: Send it to the clients | 'What if their AI and our AI just agreed on scope?' Legal is sweating.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[No blockers. No you. No problem.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[An AI that attends your daily, says 'still on the same ticket' with total confidence and takes everything offline. You stay under the duvet.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Skip standup forever]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Sounds exactly like you | Trained on 400 standups. Says 'yesterday I carried on with the thing' so naturally that the team just nods.
Takes it offline | Every hard question gets 'let's take that afterwards'. There is no afterwards. That is the feature.
Camera off by design | Shows your initials in a grey circle. Colleagues report no difference since 2021.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[My AI has attended every daily since March. Yesterday it was made team lead.
We sent nine AIs to standup. It took four seconds. Nobody knows what was decided.
It said 'no blockers' so convincingly that I believed it. I had blockers.
As scrum master I now say good morning to nine bots. They answer. That's new.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[15 minutes of your life back every day for DKK 49 a month. Enterprise: we skip the retro too.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© An AI That Goes to Standup for You. This footer was written by the AI. It has no blockers.]]></Value>
